<!--
    The mark, exactly as drawn in the "Dusk bar" concept of
    `docs/design-system/design-system.html` (rect x=40 y=24 w=28 h=64 rx=14
    + circle cx=60 cy=32 r=16): one wide waveform bar — the house language
    ("the waveform is the alphabet") kept rather than started over — with a
    crescent bitten out of its top. Read and listen stay the bar; the app's
    new name is the moon.

    The bite is a background-coloured circle painted over the bar, same
    technique as the artifact's own SVG mockup — not a fillType="evenOdd"
    subtraction. evenOdd was tried first and is wrong here: it doesn't
    subtract, it computes even/odd crossing count, so any part of the bite
    circle that falls *outside* the bar (most of it, at this radius) gets
    filled back in as a second, disconnected blob instead of vanishing.
    Painting over in the exact ground colour has no such failure mode — it's
    just two opaque shapes in draw order — at the cost of only being correct
    against a ground that really is this colour behind it, which is true
    here (splash window and adaptive-icon background are both this hex).

    Same safe-zone handling as the mark it replaces: geometry lives inside
    the outer group's 0.85 scale, which is what keeps it inside the
    66-unit zone both the launcher mask and the Android 12+ splash crop to.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <group
        android:name="mark"
        android:pivotX="54"
        android:pivotY="54"
        android:scaleX="0.85"
        android:scaleY="0.85">

        <!-- One group, one shape — the whole mark settles together in the
             splash, not bar by bar. -->
        <group
            android:name="bar_main"
            android:pivotX="54"
            android:pivotY="54">
            <path
                android:fillColor="#C6684A"
                android:pathData="M40,38 a14,14 0 0 1 28,0 v36 a14,14 0 0 1 -28,0 z" />
            <path
                android:fillColor="#101010"
                android:pathData="M44,32 a16,16 0 0 1 32,0 a16,16 0 0 1 -32,0 z" />
        </group>
    </group>
</vector>
